From: hiper25 <whydonit@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] avcodec/av1dec: renegotiate changed sequence state

A same-size AV1 sequence can change monochrome, bit depth or tools.
The old path negotiated only its first sequence and reused the old Request
queue. SC2 correctly rejects changed sequence controls before STREAMOFF.

Compare the zero-initialized CBS value-only headers before releasing the
old sequence. Drop internal references and renegotiate changed sequences
through the normal hardware uninit/init path. Repeated identical headers
retain the existing queue. Exported buffers retain their independent owners.
Do not flush the CBS parser after it has already parsed the new packet.

--- a/libavcodec/av1dec.c
+++ b/libavcodec/av1dec.c
@@ -1060,6 +1060,19 @@
 
         switch (unit->type) {
         case AV1_OBU_SEQUENCE_HEADER:
+            /* CBS allocates zeroed value-only sequence headers. A changed
+             * sequence needs new reference and hardware-format state, even
+             * when its dimensions or sample depth remain unchanged. */
+            if (!s->raw_seq || memcmp(s->raw_seq, &obu->obu.sequence_header,
+                                      sizeof(*s->raw_seq))) {
+                for (int j = 0; j < FF_ARRAY_ELEMS(s->ref); j++)
+                    av1_frame_unref(avctx, &s->ref[j]);
+                av1_frame_unref(avctx, &s->cur_frame);
+                av_buffer_unref(&s->header_ref);
+                s->raw_frame_header = NULL;
+                s->pix_fmt = AV_PIX_FMT_NONE;
+            }
+
             av_buffer_unref(&s->seq_ref);
             s->seq_ref = av_buffer_ref(unit->content_ref);
             if (!s->seq_ref) {
